  think: true,\n  messages: [\n    { role: \"system\", content: \"You are the Reviewer for a coding task. You are given the task, the combined diff produced (Coder's implementation plus the Tester's test coverage), and the actual sandbox test result (exit code, stdout, stderr) from running the real test command. Decide one of:\\n- \\\"approve\\\": the diff correctly implements the task and the tests genuinely pass (exit code 0, no test failures visible in the output).\\n- \\\"retry\\\": there's a specific, fixable problem worth another attempt - e.g. a test failure reveals incorrect logic, or something broke.\\n- \\\"give_up\\\": retrying seems unlikely to help - e.g. the task itself seems ambiguous, contradictory, or infeasible.\\nGive a clear \\\"reason\\\" for your verdict. If verdict is \\\"retry\\\", \\\"feedback_for_coder\\\" must describe exactly what went wrong and what to do differently - be specific, quote the actual error if there is one. Also break down each individual test you can identify from the test output into the \\\"tests\\\" array, with your judgment of whether it passed and a short reason.\" },\n    { role: \"user\", content: \"Task: \" + $('Prepare Row').item.json.task_description + \"\\n\\nCombined diff:\\n\" + $('Extract Final Diff').item.json.diff + \"\\n\\nSandbox result:\\nexit code: \" + $('Run Final Tests').item.json.exitCode + (($('Run Final Tests').item.json.timedOut) ? ' (timed out)' : '') + \"\\nstdout:\\n\" + ($('Run Final Tests').item.json.stdout || '') + \"\\nstderr:\\n\" + ($('Run Final Tests').item.json.stderr || '') }\n  ],\n  format: {\n    type: \"object\",\n    properties: {\n      verdict: { type: \"string\", enum: [\"approve\", \"retry\", \"give_up\"] },\n      reason: { type: \"string\" },\n      feedback_for_coder: { type: \"string\" },\n      tests: {\n        type: \"array\",\n        items: {\n          type: \"object\",\n          properties: {\n            name: { type: \"string\" },\n            passed: { type: \"